# A Website in a Website

This card is a whole website, and the program beside it is all of it. Change a
line and the page rebuilds as you type: the words, the list, the button, the colours.

## Page /

State:
    Let hellos be 0.
    Let dark be false.
    Let reasons be ["You can read every line.", "Logic and mathematics are built in.", "Your agent writes it with you."].

Actions:
    To wave:
        Set hellos to hellos + 1.

    To switchLights:
        Set dark to not dark.

View:
    <section id="site" class="site" class:dark={dark}>
      <p class="kicker">Made with LOGOS</p>
      <h1 id="title">A website in a website</h1>
      <p>Everything on this card is the English program beside it.</p>
      <ul>
        {for each reason in reasons:}
          <li>{reason}</li>
        {end}
      </ul>
      <div class="row">
        <button id="wave" on-click={wave}>Say hello</button>
        <button id="lights" class="secondary" on-click={switchLights}>Switch the lights</button>
      </div>
      <p id="hellos" class="count">{hellos | plural "hello" "hellos"} so far</p>
    </section>

Style:
    .kicker { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 0.25rem; }
    .row { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.75rem; margin: 1.25rem 0 0.75rem; }
    .count { color: var(--muted); margin: 0; }
    .site.dark { background: #1f1e1d; color: #f5f4ef; border-color: #3a3936; }
    .site.dark .count { color: #a3a29e; }
    .site.dark .secondary { color: #f5f4ef; border-color: #3a3936; }

## Test: every hello is counted

Click "#wave".
Click "#wave".
Expect that the text of "#hellos" is equal to "2 hellos so far".

## Test: the lights switch off and on

Click "#lights".
Expect that the count of ".dark" is equal to 1.
Click "#lights".
Expect that the count of ".dark" is equal to 0.
